Usage: ./ifm <options>
GENERAL options:
    -h, --help                    This help.

INPUT options:
    -c, --cellsize=SIZE           DEM cell size, in meters (default: 90)
    -d, --dem=FILE                DEM file
    -l, --landuse=<FILE|VALUE>    Landuse file or uniform value
    -L, --landuse-map=FILE        Landuse file (optional)
    -m, --mask=FILE               Mask file
    -n, --nodata=VALUE            Extra NoData value. Can be entered multiple times (default: take from DEM)
    -o, --outlet=FILE             Outlet file (optional)
    -O, --outdir=DIR              Output directory (default: ./)
    -p, --precipitation=FILE      Precipitation file
    -w, --watch=FILE              Optional list of coordinates to watch
    -H, --soil-hc=<FILE|VALUE>    Soil hydraulic conductivity file or uniform value
    -P, --soil-ph=<FILE|VALUE>    Soil pressure head file or uniform value
    -E, --soil-ep=<FILE|VALUE>    Soil effective porosity file or uniform value
    -M, --soil-moisture=<FILE|VALUE> Soil moisture file or uniform value (default: 0.0)

MODIFIERS:
    -1, --soil-ep-multiplier=VALUE   Multiply soil-ep grid points by VALUE (default: 1.0)
    -2, --soil-hc-multiplier=VALUE   Multiply soil-hc grid points by VALUE (default: 1.0)
    -3, --soil-ph-multiplier=VALUE   Multiply soil-ph grid points by VALUE (default: 1.0)

OUTPUT options:
    -r, --output-rate=NUM_SECONDS How often to output depth files (default: 300)
    -V, --output-vars=VARIABLES   Comma-separated list of variables to save. Accepted arguments are:
                                  depth, flowrate, olr, vsat, maxvolume. (default: depth)

SIMULATION options:
    -b, --tbegin    =NUM_SECONDS   Simulation start time (default: 0)
    -f, --tfinal    =NUM_SECONDS   Simulation end time (default: 1800)
    -i, --infiltrate=BOOLEAN <0|1> Conduct infiltration stage (default: 1)
    -t, --profile   =BOOLEAN <0|1> Profile code (default: 0)
    -s, --tstep     =NUM_SECONDS   Time step in seconds (default: 1)
    -S, --state     =FILE          Save/restore simulation state from the given file

UNIFORM precipitation file example:
0    100
3599 100
3600 0

NETCDF precipitation file example:
0       wrfout_d04_2010-04-07_00:00:00
600     wrfout_d04_2010-04-07_00:10:00
1200    wrfout_d04_2010-04-07_00:20:00

OUTLET file example:
1 1 0.003539

WATCH file example:
# Lat Lon : Location name
-81.584575 28.413437 : Walt Disney World

